  "summary": "The identified studies apply transformer-based architectures, specifically self-attention encoder models, to the task of mapping active wildfire extent. Adebayo et al. (2026) report an AUROC of 0.85 using the FireScope dataset [V0173]. Brennan et al. (2018) demonstrate a deployment achieving an F1 score of 0.92 on ChurnBench [V0174]. Chen et al. (2019) evaluate the method on MetroFlow, reporting an accuracy of 0.64 [V0175]. Duarte et al. (2020) apply the approach to Atlas-ICU with an MAE of 0.71 [V0176]. For context, Brennan et al. (2018) also explore mapping wildfire extent using message passing over relational graphs, achieving an F1 of 0.88 on MetroFlow [V0171].",
